{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}About{% endblock %}

{% block main_class %}grow bg-gray-950{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div data-controller="aos">

    {# ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute inset-0"
             style="background: url({{ asset('images/martian_landscape.webp') }}) center center no-repeat; background-size: cover;">
        </div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-950/80 via-gray-950/60 to-gray-950"></div>
        <div class="relative text-center px-6 pt-20 sm:pt-28 pb-12 sm:pb-16">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">About</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">Adam Ashmore</h1>
            <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-xl mx-auto">
                Co-founder of Ebuyer.com, lifelong coder, and the person behind SupplyMars.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── The Project ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-950 pt-8 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p>
                    SupplyMars is a working demonstration of how I think, how I build and how I approach complex problems. It models real back-office e-commerce operations: multi-supplier sourcing, dynamic pricing, order fulfilment and reporting, with live data flowing through it every day.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I chose e-commerce because I spent fifteen years building one of the UK's largest online retailers, and wanted to revisit familiar problems with hindsight and a clean sheet.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I am now looking for interesting work, bringing hands-on engineering, commercial understanding and experience of building systems that businesses depend on.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── About Me ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-900 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
            <div class="text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">About Me</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
                    25+ Years Building Software
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    Most of my career has been spent building things end to end: working directly with the people who needed the software, understanding their problems, and turning those into working systems.
                </p>
                <p>
                    That has involved writing code, shaping products, building teams and helping developers grow. I enjoy the detail of implementation as much as the wider challenge of deciding what to build and how to make it useful.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Some of the work I am proudest of has come from close collaboration. SupplyMars is a solo project by choice: modern tooling made it possible, and it felt too exciting not to try.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Background: Ebuyer ───────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-950 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
            <div class="mb-12 lg:mb-16" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">Background</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg mt-6">
                    I wrote my first program at age 9 on a ZX81, and have never really stopped. With a degree in Electronic Engineering, I spent several years working in electronics, designing high-performance components for military, aerospace and industrial applications. In 1998, I moved fully into software, building web tools at a UK internet service provider.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-12 lg:mb-16" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">1999&ndash;2014</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
                    Ebuyer.com
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    In late 1999, I co-founded Ebuyer.com, an online retailer of computer and electrical goods. In the early years, I was the sole developer, building both the customer-facing website and the full suite of tools covering procurement, product management, customer service, logistics, fulfilment, returns, accounting, marketing and analytics, all on a LAMP stack. This was 2000, long before frameworks, cloud services or payment platforms made any of it easy.
                </p>
                <p>
                    MySQL was at the heart of everything. I designed the database from the schema up, wrote the reporting queries and summary tables the business ran on, and became deeply proficient in performance tuning as data and traffic grew.
                </p>
            </div>

            {# Key metrics - subtle, not CV-like #}
            <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 text-center">
                    <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">&pound;300m+</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Annual Turnover</p>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 text-center">
                    <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">200+</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Staff</p>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 text-center">
                    <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-1">1m+</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Customers</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-12 space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    I saw that growth at every stage. In the early days, that meant building something from scratch, the excitement of watching the first orders come in, celebrating when we reached 100 in a single day, and still helping pick, pack and answer customer calls. Later it meant the scale and automation of shipping 10,000 boxes per day across multiple warehouses and couriers, and watching the last trucks leave each evening.
                </p>
                <p class="text-gray-300">
                    Ebuyer was acquired in 2004. I chose to stay for another decade.
                </p>
                <p>
                    As the company grew from five people to one of the UK's largest online retailers, I built the team around the platform: developers, designers, sysadmins, DBAs and technical support. As IT Director I led and mentored them, oversaw most of our projects and features, and stayed hands-on in the code. We worked in fast, iterative cycles, shipping early, gathering feedback and improving continuously. Code reviews, shared ownership and close collaboration with non-technical teams were how we operated.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Throughout all of that, what I valued most was the direct relationship with the people using the software: sitting with each department to understand how they worked, then building the tools that made them faster. That pattern shaped how I think about software to this day.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Background: Wren Kitchens ────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-900 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
            <div class="mb-12 lg:mb-16" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">2009</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
                    Wren Kitchens
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    In 2009, we adapted the Ebuyer codebase to launch Wren Kitchens, taking a platform built for online retail and reshaping it for a completely different business model. As of 2022, Wren had over 100 showrooms, 6,000 employees and annual turnover above &pound;1.25 billion, and the platform played its part.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Background: Since 2014 ───────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-950 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
            <div class="mb-12 lg:mb-16" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">Since 2014</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
                    Still Building
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    The sale of Ebuyer gave me the freedom to step back and raise a young family. But I never stopped building. I kept coding, kept learning, and continued developing with modern frameworks, cleaner architecture, automated testing, containerised workflows and CI/CD.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Some things I used years ago have been replaced by better alternatives; others remain exactly the right tools. What matters is knowing what fits, and why.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Now that my children are older, I am ready to return to a team and take responsibility for meaningful work again. I want to stay hands-on, work with good people and make full use of my experience.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── What I Bring ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="relative bg-gray-900 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_80%_50%_at_50%_0%,rgba(120,119,198,0.04),transparent)]"></div>

        <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-(--breakpoint-xl) px-6">
            <div class="mb-16 lg:mb-20 text-center" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">What I Bring</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-6">
                    A Broad Range of Skills
                </h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
                    Much of my career has involved work that many organisations would spread across several roles. The specific tools in this project are only part of the picture.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="0">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-orange-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:lightbulb-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-orange-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Product Thinking</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Understanding what matters, what does not, and what the software is actually there to do.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-violet-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:diagram-3-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-violet-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Technical Architecture</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Designing systems that are clear, maintainable, and suited to the real problem.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:code-slash" class="h-6 w-6 text-blue-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Software Engineering</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Currently PHP and Symfony, but the discipline (domain modelling, APIs, async workflows, testing) transfers across stacks.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:database-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-cyan-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Database Design</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Deep experience with MySQL, from schema design and SQL to reporting and performance.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-pink-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:palette-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-pink-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">UI/UX</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Interfaces that are clear, task-focused, and built for people who need to get things done.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="250">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:window-desktop" class="h-6 w-6 text-amber-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Front-end Development</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Currently Tailwind and Hotwire, but the underlying concern is speed, clarity and usability.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="0">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:shield-check" class="h-6 w-6 text-emerald-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">QA &amp; Testing</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Quality built in through automated tests, static analysis, code review and sensible discipline.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-sky-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:cloud-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-sky-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">DevOps &amp; Infrastructure</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Docker, CI/CD, AWS, queues and caching, plus years of managing bare-metal LAMP stacks.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:bar-chart-line-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-indigo-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Data &amp; Reporting</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Reporting, dashboards, summary models, segmentation, and a strong instinct for what operational data is actually useful.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-teal-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:chat-dots-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-teal-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Communication</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Explaining trade-offs clearly and translating between technical and non-technical concerns.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-rose-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:gear-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-rose-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Operations &amp; Process</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Systems shaped around real workflows, not abstract diagrams.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="group rounded-xl bg-gray-800/40 ring-1 ring-white/[0.06] p-6 transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-gray-800/60 hover:ring-white/[0.1]" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="250">
                    <div class="mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-fuchsia-500/10">
                        <twig:ux:icon name="bi:people-fill" class="h-6 w-6 text-fuchsia-400" />
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Leadership &amp; Mentoring</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Building teams, mentoring developers, and helping people improve along with the software.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-16 mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg text-center" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p>
                    Sometimes that means being hands-on across a broad range; sometimes it means working with specialists and seeing the bigger picture. I am comfortable taking a project from an initial conversation through to a running system, or stepping into an existing team where broad experience and judgement are useful.
                </p>
                <p>
                    How software is delivered matters as much as how it is written. Fast iteration, refactoring, automated testing, clean version control and sensible tooling are part of doing the work properly.
                </p>
                <p>
                    You can explore the engineering behind SupplyMars on <a href="https://github.com/myvars/supplymars" target="_blank" class="text-orange-400 hover:text-orange-300 transition-colors focus-ring">GitHub</a>, including the architecture decisions, test suite and infrastructure.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── Why Now ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="bg-gray-950 py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center">
            <div class="mb-8" data-aos="fade-up">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4">Why Now</p>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
                    Software Is Changing Again
                </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed text-base lg:text-lg" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    AI tooling shortens the distance between an idea and a working system, but it does not remove the need for experience. If anything, it makes judgement more important: understanding the problem properly, choosing what matters, keeping the design clear, and knowing when something is good enough.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I wrote most of SupplyMars by hand, with AI as an assistant. My workflow has since evolved, and AI now generates much of the code I write. I remain responsible for the architecture, the decisions and the result: understanding the implementation, reviewing changes, testing behaviour and making sure the system remains maintainable.
                </p>
                <p class="text-gray-300">
                    That combination of experience and new tools makes this a particularly exciting time to be building software. SupplyMars is one example of how I put it into practice.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {# ── CTA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <section class="relative py-28 lg:py-36 overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-950 to-gray-900"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_50%_at_50%_50%,rgba(249,115,22,0.04),transparent)]"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-[0.04]"
             style="background-image: url({{ asset('images/martian_landscape.webp') }}); background-size: cover; background-position: center;">
        </div>

        <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange-500 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up">Get in Touch</p>
            <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-3"
                data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50" data-aos-duration="600">
                Let's Talk
            </h2>
            <p class="text-base font-medium text-gray-500 tracking-wide mb-8" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="75">
                Adam Ashmore
            </p>
            <div class="space-y-5 text-lg text-gray-400 mb-12 leading-relaxed" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                <p>
                    I am looking for interesting, ambitious work with good people, where the software makes a tangible difference. That could be a senior or lead engineering role, a founding engineer at an early-stage company, or hands-on technical leadership.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I am interested in permanent or contract opportunities, working remotely. If that sounds like something you are working on, I would be glad to hear from you.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                <a href="mailto:contact@supplymars.com"
                   class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-7 py-3 text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-white bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-400 rounded-lg shadow-lg shadow-orange-500/25 transition-all duration-200 active:scale-[0.98]">
                    <twig:ux:icon name="bi:envelope-fill" class="h-5 w-5" />
                    Get in Touch
                </a>
                <a href="{{ path('app_catalog_product_index') }}"
                   class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-7 py-3 text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-gray-300 bg-white/[0.06] hover:bg-white/[0.1] rounded-lg ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] hover:ring-white/[0.18] transition-all duration-200 active:scale-[0.98]"
                   data-turbo-prefetch="false">
                    Explore the Platform
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/myvars/supplymars"
                   target="_blank"
                   class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-7 py-3 text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-gray-300 bg-white/[0.06] hover:bg-white/[0.1] rounded-lg ring-1 ring-white/[0.1] hover:ring-white/[0.18] transition-all duration-200 active:scale-[0.98]">
                    <twig:ux:icon name="bi:github" class="h-5 w-5" />
                    View on GitHub
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    </div>
{% endblock %}
